### Mental Health Reporting Requirements in South Australia

#### **1. Mental Health Act 2009 (SA)**
- **Mandatory Reporting**: Health practitioners must report certain incidents involving mental health clients, including:
  - **Serious Adverse Events**: Any event that results in serious harm or death of a mental health client [1](https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.sa.gov.au/legislation/mental-health-act/forms).
  - **Use of Restraint or Seclusion**: Any instance where restraint or seclusion is used must be documented and reported [1](https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.sa.gov.au/legislation/mental-health-act/forms).

#### **2. Office of the Chief Psychiatrist Policies**
- **Critical Incidents**: Any incident that has a significant impact on the health and safety of a mental health client must be reported to the Chief Psychiatrist [2](https://www.sahealth.sa.gov.au/wps/wcm/connect/public+content/sa+health+internet/about+us/legislation/mental+health+act+2009).
- **Annual Reporting**: Health services must submit annual reports on the use of restraint and seclusion, as well as other key metrics related to mental health care [2](https://www.sahealth.sa.gov.au/wps/wcm/connect/public+content/sa+health+internet/about+us/legislation/mental+health+act+2009).

#### **3. Additional Reporting Requirements**
- **Electroconvulsive Treatment (ECT)**: Mental health services must report the use of ECT and any adverse events related to its administration [3](https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.sa.gov.au/legislation/mental-health-act).
- **Deaths in Care**: Any death of a person receiving mental health care must be reported to the Chief Psychiatrist [3](https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.sa.gov.au/legislation/mental-health-act).
- **Sexual Safety Incidents**: Reporting any incidents related to the sexual safety of mental health clients [3](https://www.chiefpsychiatrist.sa.gov.au/legislation/mental-health-act).

These requirements ensure comprehensive documentation, transparency, and accountability within the mental health care system, aiming to improve the safety and quality of care provided to mental health clients in South Australia.

